nk about the dynamic of  him being around his mother because she  seems like she runs things in that house  i also thought it felt like bob odenkirk  found a new layer for his character in  this scene not gene but not exactly saul  or jimmy either he's there to pull jeff  in but still jabs at him using his own  words enough to make it sting later he  tells him here's the deal i will show  you the game and then we're done and  from there we see him put together his  multi-part plant and just to get into  the spirit of things he pulls out  marco's pinky ring and wears it for the  duration of this scam phase one is to  make friends with the nighttime security  guards and find out how long he can  distract the one who's watching the  cameras by giving him free cinnabun it's  a lot of fun to watch as gene works his  way in here the first guard remembers  him telling the shoplifter to call a  lawyer back in season three you see how  he lightens up a little with each  cinnamon roll gene makes friends with  his partner who is the real mark since  he's the one he has to distract from the  monitors he throws himself into research  in college football after just echoing  his reactions to the game in their first  conversation there's been a question  about if the gene timeline happens in  2010 or 2011. while they're talking they  mention a martinez setting a freshman  record and that's something that really  happened in october of 2010. saul used  ed to disappear from albuquerque in  april of that year which means he's been  living as gene for about six months if  you're one of those people who were  holding out hope that walter white might  still be alive in the gene timeline this  should put that to rest since he died in  september phase two is to go to the  mall's department store lancasters and  locate the most expensive items that  jeff could grab in the time it takes  frank to savor his nightly treat you see  gene counting the steps from the  different items much like gus did with  his gun in the lab but here he isn't  planning to find something in the dark  he's planning on making a training  course he runs jeff around that while  shouting a rhyme he's come up with to  help him remember what to grab over a  bullhorn and there isn't any question  that this is a very well thought out  plan still it seems crazy to jeff and  gene has to pull out the story of walter  white to motivate him to continue he  leaves out all the terrible stuff that  happened and just says i'll tell you  what's crazy 50 year old high school  chemistry teacher comes into my office  the guy is so broke he can't pay his own  mortgage one year later he's got a pile  of cash as big as a volkswagen phase  three is to get jeff into the building  inside a wooden crate that can then  later be used to stash the loot until  the next morning he sweet talks the  store manager when she calls to complain  and then everything is set when frank  starts eating his cinnabon gene texts  jeff that it's time to go he comes out  of the crate and does just as he  rehearsed on the practice field until he  runs into a snag there was a scuff mark  on the floor so the manager kathy had  called to have it cleaned up and when  jeff ran across it he slipped and fell  he actually knocked himself out so gene  has to think on his feet because frank's  almost done eating and he always  immediately turns around to check the  monitors where he would be able to  clearly see jeff lying motionless in the  middle of the store he does something  that we've seen him do before he starts  to spin a tale that is mostly based in  truth he starts to cry saying that his  parents are dead his brother is dead he  has no wife no kids no friends and all  of this makes you think of chuck and kim  and it's pretty heavy you know that on  some level it's just an act but in a way  this is the most emotion he's shown  about chuck's death he's built up enough  of a rapport that frank is sympathetic  and i thought it was a nice touch that  when he asks him if he knows what he  means he's like no not me because that  shows that it might be awkward enough  that it wouldn't be weird if gene no  longer comes to visit anymore it works  long enough to give jeff time to get up  and to go hide in the bathroom until the  morning we see him sneak out as the  delivery worker comes to pick up the  crate and it looks like they're gonna  get away with it  jeff and his friend are pumped up but  gene brings them some bad news he tells  them all of the crimes that they've  committed and explains the concept of  mutually assured destruction they can no  longer threaten to turn him in because  if he goes down he'll take them with him  as he's driving this home he echoes  their first meeting in the mall when he  says say it and tells them they're not  friends they're done and not to come  back looking for more they seem to  understand that they've lost and there's  one more close call when marion comes  home where jean is able to pretend like  he's fixing the car to create a cover  story he helps her inside with her  groceries and she explains that she's  happy that he's in jeff's life because  he fell in with a bad crowd in  albuquerque and she thinks that he's  doing better now that he has him in his  life she also asks him about nippy and  it almost catches him off guard he tells  her that he got him back and he says the  line we heard a few weeks ago in the  teaser trailer after all that a happy  ending from there we see him go back to  work and he looks alive again we've seen  him do this so many times in those cold  open teasers but here he is actually  smiling he's so into it he almost  forgets to go to lunch but when reminded  he goes over to lancaster's and you can  see that he knows that they got away  with it you see him with a look on his  face where it's almost as if he's  impressed with himself and how he's able  to pull this off without any unintended  consequences he looks around the 