t sure what problem he needs to  solve other than he's living a boring  paranoid life and there's not much he  can do about the second part of that  restraint isn't an option it's necessary  so if he can have a taste and walk away  from it what does that say about his  character at this point in the story the  other decision that stood out was to  cast carol burnett as jeff's overbearing  but ultimately harmless mother it would  be fine if that was all they asked her  to do watching her spit out the  wisconsin extra sharp cheddar that had  writer producer tom schnauz's name  attached to it was one of many great  little moments but i don't know because  in that final scene in the kitchen i  kept expecting her to turn on gene it  would be hilarious if she tried to turn  his life upside down for what he did to  her jeffy there could be an epic  showdown there to end the series the two  actors were great working together so it  feels like there's more potential there  if they decided to go that route this is  all informed by the fact that i think  making him face what he's done makes the  most sense for the character's ending  i've wanted to believe that there was  some jimmy still inside there after the  events of breaking bad and this episode  showed that at least the part where he  can make people like him when he needs  to is there if the good parts are there  too then there's a chance at redemption  but it seems like it has to come be a  reckoning of the harm he caused and  looking at some of the things that he's  kept buried could marian force him to  move in that direction if she makes his  life complicated does it make more sense  for it to be something related to kim  and how will walt and jesse making an  appearance fit in these are great  questions to have because this is the  only show that i can imagine putting me  in a place to absolutely have no idea at  the end of the day it feels like a flex  because it seems like they had an idea  that was so good that