nk about the dynamic of  him being around his mother because she  seems like she runs things in that house  i also thought it felt like bob odenkirk  found a new layer for his character in  this scene not gene but not exactly saul  or jimmy either he's there to pull jeff  in but still jabs at him using his own  words enough to make it sting later he  tells him here's the deal i will show  you the game and then we're done and  from there we see him put together his  multi-part plant and just to get into  the spirit of things he pulls out  marco's pinky ring and wears it for the  duration of this scam phase one is to  make friends with the nighttime security  guards and find out how long he can  distract the one who's watching the  cameras by giving him free cinnabun it's  a lot of fun to watch as gene works his  way in here the first guard remembers  him telling the shoplifter to call a  lawyer back in season three you see how  he lightens up a little with each  cinnamon roll gene makes friends with  his partner who is the real mark since  he's the one he has to distract from the  monitors he throws himself into research  in college football after just echoing  his reactions to the game in their first  conversation there's been a question  about if the gene timeline happens in  2010 or 2011. while they're talking they  mention a martinez setting a freshman  record and that's something that really  happened in october of 2010. saul used  ed to disappear from albuquerque in  april of that year which means he's been  living as gene for about six months if  you're one of those people who were  holding out hope that walter white might  still be alive in the gene timeline this  should put that to rest since he died in  september phase two is to go to the  mall's department store lancasters and  locate the most expensive items that  jeff could grab in the time it takes  frank to savor his nightly treat you see  gene counting the steps from the  different items much like gus did with  his gun in the lab but here he isn't  planning to find something in the dark  he's planning on making a training  course he runs jeff around that while  shouting a rhyme he's come up with to  help him remember what to grab over a  bullhorn and there isn't any question  that this is a very well thought out  plan still it seems crazy to jeff and  gene has to pull out the story of walter  white to motivate him to continue he  leaves out all the terrible stuff that  happened and just says i'll tell you  what's crazy 50 year old high school  chemistry teacher comes into my office  the guy is so broke he can't pay his own  mortgage one year later he's got a pile  of cash as big as a volkswagen phase  three is to get jeff into the building  inside a wooden crate that can then  later be used to stash the loot until  the next morning he sweet talks the  store manager when she calls to complain  and then everything is set when frank  starts eating his cinnabon gene texts  jeff that it's time to go he comes out  of the crate and does just as he  rehearsed on the practice field until he  runs into a snag there was a scuff mark  on the floor so the manager kathy had  called to have it cleaned up and when  jeff ran across it he slipped and fell  he actually knocked himself out so gene  has to think on his feet because frank's  almost done eating and he always  immediately turns around to check the  monitors where he would be able to  clearly see jeff lying motionless in the  middle of the store he does something  that we've seen him do before he starts  to spin a tale that is mostly based in  truth he starts to cry saying that his  parents are dead his brother is dead he  has no wife no kids no friends and all  of this makes you think of chuck and kim  and it's pretty heavy you know that on  some level it's just an act but in a way  this is the most emotion he's shown  about chuck's death he's built up enough  of a rapport that frank is sympathetic  and i thought it was a nice touch that  when he asks him if he knows what he  means he's like no not me because that  shows that it might be awkward enough  that it wouldn't be weird if gene no  longer comes to visit anymore it works  long enough to give jeff time to get up  and to go hide in the bathroom until the  morning we see him sneak out as the  delivery worker comes to pick up the  crate and it looks like they're gonna  get away with it  jeff and his friend are pumped up but  gene brings them some bad news he tells  them all of the crimes that they've  committed and explains the concept of  mutually assured destruction they can no  longer threaten to turn him in because  if he goes down he'll take them with him  as he's driving this home he echoes  their first meeting in the mall when he  says say it and tells them they're not  friends they're done and not to come  back looking for more they seem to  understand that they've lost and there's  one more close call when marion comes  home where jean is able to pretend like  he's fixing the car to create a cover  story he helps her inside with her  groceries and she explains that she's  happy that he's in jeff's life because  he fell in with a bad crowd in  albuquerque and she thinks that he's  doing better now that he has him in his  life she also asks him about nippy and  it almost catches him off guard he tells  her that he got him back and he says the  line we heard a few weeks ago in the  teaser trailer after all that a happy  ending from there we see him go back to  work and he looks alive again we've seen  him do this so many times in those cold  open teasers but here he is actually  smiling he's so into it he almost  forgets to go to lunch but when reminded  he goes over to lancaster's and you can  see that he knows that they got away  with it you see him with a look on his  face where it's almost as if he's  impressed with himself and how he's able  to pull this off without any unintended  consequences he looks around the store  he picks up a loud shirt and tie combo  he holds it up and looks at himself in  the mirror and then he puts it down and  walks away as the episode comes to an  end so my initial thought was that even  though this is a great episode of better  call saul that continued to deliver the  inevitable in a way we couldn't quite  predict i was so perplexed that he  pulled everything off that it almost  seemed like there was something missing  as i went back and re-watched to put  these notes together knowing what would  happen it stood out just how true to  what we've seen for six seasons this was  it may have been in black and white and  we may have gotten the answer to how  he'd take down jeff but what's more  exciting is that feeling of not knowing  what comes next we heard most of the  remaining sound bites from those  mid-season break teaser trailers we got  a classic scam quite a few laughs a nice  split screen montage and enough  references to reward us for paying  attention that it almost seemed like a  reset but if that's the case seriously  where do we go from here this isn't how  i would choose the end jeans story but  it could certainly feel like an ending  if we didn't know there were three more  episodes there are two choices that  stand out to me here the first is that  he got away with the scam and out from  under jeff clean in my last couple of  videos i've been talking about addiction  as it relates to jimmy and kim and their  scamming in sobriety they say the drink  or drug that will take you down is the  one you get away with because that gives  you the false sense that you don't need  to abstain even though it remains in  black and white it's almost like you can  see the color come back into his life at  the end but then he puts the saul s  closed down and walks away this episode  shows that he'll never be happy as gene  but also hasn't slipped completely into  his old ways either that could mean that  he'll take on a brand new persona but  i'm not sure what problem he needs to  solve other than he's living a boring  paranoid life and there's not much he  can do about the second part of that  restraint isn't an option it's necessary  so if he can have a taste and walk away  from it what does that say about his  character at this point in the story the  other decision that stood out was to  cast carol burnett as jeff's overbearing  but ultimately harmless mother it would  be fine if that was all they asked her  to do watching her spit out the  wisconsin extra sharp cheddar that had  writer producer tom schnauz's name  attached to it was one of many great  little moments but i don't know because  in that final scene in the kitchen i  kept expecting her to turn on gene it  would be hilarious if she tried to turn  his life upside down for what he did to  her jeffy there could be an epic  showdown there to end the series the two  actors were great working together so it  feels like there's more potential there  if they decided to go that route this is  all informed by the fact that i think  making him face what he's done makes the  most sense for the character's ending  i've wanted to believe that there was  some jimmy still inside there after the  events of breaking bad and this episode  showed that at least the part where he  can make people like him when he needs  to is there if the good parts are there  too then there's a chance at redemption  but it seems like it has to come be a  reckoning of the harm he caused and  looking at some of the things that he's  kept buried could marian force him to  move in that direction if she makes his  life complicated does it make more sense  for it to be something related to kim  and how will walt and jesse making an  appearance fit in these are great  questions to have because this is the  only show that i can imagine putting me  in a place to absolutely have no idea at  the end of the day it feels like a flex  because it seems like they had an idea  that was so good that they thought this  was the best way to go about it and i  want to know what that is i can't wait  to find out and i think that is a good  place to leave things join us for the  live stream on tuesday night at 9 pm  eastern time we'll get into more of what  we're thinking about after we had a  little bit of time let me know in the  comments what you thought about this  episode where you think things are going  what stood out to you the most was it  marion was it jimmy shedding a tear  while he was talking about chuck or was  it seeing him put the clothes back up on  the rack and walk away please like this  video if you enjoyed it please subscribe  to my channel if you haven't already and  thanks for watching i'll talk to you  soon  you


